WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.634
Hi! Which is bigger, one half or two quarters? They're actually the same! Today we'll learn equivalent fractions and simplest form.

2
00:00:11.784 --> 00:00:19.794
Look at these three strips of the same length. The shaded parts are the same: one half, two quarters, four eighths.

3
00:00:19.944 --> 00:00:25.554
These fractions are equal in size. They're called equivalent fractions.

4
00:00:25.704 --> 00:00:31.770
Multiply the numerator and the denominator by 2, and one half becomes two quarters.

5
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:38.490
Two thirds: multiply top and bottom by 3 to get six ninths.

6
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.538
Can six eighths be made simpler?

7
00:00:41.688 --> 00:00:45.306
Both 6 and 8 can be divided by 2.

8
00:00:45.456 --> 00:00:49.698
Divide top and bottom by 2, and we get three quarters.

9
00:00:49.848 --> 00:00:58.002
3 and 4 can't both be divided by any number except 1, so three quarters is in simplest form.

10
00:00:58.152 --> 00:01:07.554
Watch out! Some pupils think adding 1 to the top and bottom gives an equal fraction, so one half equals two thirds. That's wrong!

11
00:01:07.704 --> 00:01:13.602
To get an equivalent fraction, we can only multiply or divide both by the same number.

12
00:01:13.752 --> 00:01:18.930
One half, multiplied by 2, is two quarters.

13
00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:27.570
Your turn! Two fifths equals how many tenths? Pause and think.

14
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:37.410
The denominator 5 times 2 is 10, so the numerator 2 times 2 is 4. Four tenths. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:46.338
Another one! Write four twelfths in simplest form. Pause and think.

16
00:01:46.488 --> 00:01:55.242
Both 4 and 12 can be divided by 4. Divide both and we get one third. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:55.392 --> 00:02:04.386
Here's another! Three fifths equals how many fifteenths? Pause and think.

18
00:02:04.536 --> 00:02:13.386
5 times 3 is 15, so 3 times 3 is 9. Nine fifteenths. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:13.536 --> 00:02:22.266
Try one more! Write eight tenths in simplest form. Pause and think.

20
00:02:22.416 --> 00:02:28.530
Divide both by 2 to get four fifths. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:37.242
Last one! Are five tenths and one half equal? Pause and think.

22
00:02:37.392 --> 00:02:46.074
Divide five tenths by 5 on top and bottom, and we get one half. They're equal. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:46.224 --> 00:02:57.282
Remember: multiply or divide the top and bottom by the same number and the fraction stays the same size. When they can't both be divided any more, it's in simplest form.

24
00:02:57.432 --> 00:03:02.682
When you cut a cake, think of one half and two quarters!

